        "original_id": "b12d67f4-d66c-5c1a-9320-7da98f240b40",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rudolf Sieczyński, Stanley Kubrick, Arthur Schnitzler\n- Works: Vienna, City of My Dreams, Eyes Wide Shut, Traumnovelle\n- Places: Vienna, New York City\n\nFacts:\n- Rudolf Sieczyński composed and wrote the lyrics for the 1914 song \"Vienna, City of My Dreams\" (German: \"Wien, du Stadt meiner Träume\").\n- Arthur Schnitzler wrote the 1926 novella \"Traumnovelle\" (\"Dream Story\").\n- Stanley Kubrick's film \"Eyes Wide Shut\" was based on Arthur Schnitzler's 1926 novella \"Traumnovelle\" and moved the story from early 20th century Vienna to 1990s New York City.\n- Rudolf Sieczyński's song \"Vienna, City of My Dreams\" was featured in the soundtrack of Stanley Kubrick's film \"Eyes Wide Shut\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
